--- tools/sparkle/README.md
+++ tools/sparkle/README.md
@@ -62,9 +63,13 @@ sparkled lesson, so re-run `check_lesson.py` on all of them (`grep -l 'id="fs-da
 | `passiton` | Part 4 "Pass it on?" (13-01): guess for each parent trait whether it passes to the babies, ▶ Next generation reveals the babies' photo and why, then a chip question. `{afterText, kicker, title, todo[], why, parent:{name,img,alt}, kids:{name,img,alt}, yes, no, traits:[{id,icon,t,short,pass,why}], nextBtn, q, opts, credit, win, clue}` |
 | `pollen` | Warm-Up "Pollen pass" (13-02): drag (or tap, then tap a flower) the bee photo token from the `start` flower to the others; flowers of `kind` get pollinated (🌰), look-alikes of another kind show their `miss`. Then a chip question. `{afterText, kicker, title, todo[], why, hint, bee:{img,alt}, start, kind, flowers:[{id,name,img,alt,kind,miss,t}], wrongKind, startLine, again, done, countWord, q, opts, credit, win, clue}` |
 | `bagtest` | Part 1 "The bag test" (13-02): each flower head gets Open or Mesh bag, ▶ shows a seed grid (`total` seeds, `open.seeds` / `bag.seeds` full), needs at least one of each (fair test), then two chip questions. `{afterText, kicker, title, model, todo[], why, img, alt, credit, heads:[{id,name}], open:{label,seeds,note}, bag:{label,seeds,note}, total, runBtn, needBoth, q1, opts1, q2, opts2, win, clue}` |
+| `nextup` | Warm-Up "What comes next?" (14-01): a stage photo in the Now box, drag/tap the next stage into the slot; the strip fills and closes the circle, then a chip question. `{afterText, kicker, title, todo[], why, stages:[{id,t,img,alt,miss?}], whys:[one per step], hint, q, opts:[{t,ok,miss}], credit, win, clue}` |
+| `morph` | "Side by side" (14-01): a day slider; two lanes of real photos change stage (`frames:[{d,img,alt,stage,like,note}]`, `like` = looks like its parent); students must visit each day in `checks`, then a chip question. `{afterText, kicker, title, todo[], why, start, max, checks[], lanes:[{name,parent,frames}], q, opts, credit, win, clue}` |
+| `wheel` | "Close the circle" (14-01), replaces `#tab-lesson .diagram-wrap`: organism tabs; stage 1 is placed, drag/tap the rest in order onto a circle of spots, the last arrow closes the loop, then stamp the kind of cycle. `{replace, kicker, title, todo[], why, kinds:[{k,icon,t}], orgs:[{id,name,icon,stages:[{t,img,alt}],kind,kindMiss,why}], credit, win, clue}` |
+| `venn` | "Alike and different" (14-01 Part 4): pick a pair, drag/tap fact cards into Only A / Both / Only B, then a chip question per pair; the clue comes with the first finished pair. `{afterText, kicker, title, todo[], why, pairs:[{id,a:{name,img,alt},b:{…},cards:[{t,z:'a'|'both'|'b',miss}],q,opts,done}], credit, win, clue}` |
 | `exploreMod` | which game's story paragraph gets the `explore` video slot in a lean lesson (default `sort`; 10-02: `trend`) |
 | `ambient` | `{icon, label}` for the header sound pill (default 🦗 Marsh sounds) |
-| `tool` | Tool of the Week (sims so far: `trailcam` 12-01, `thermometer` (cut), `berlese` 10-01 = `tool.berlese:{title,todo,parts,predict,predictFirst,days,critters,meetWin}`, `secchi` 10-02 = `tool.secchi:{title,todo,parts:[{label,t}],sites:[{k,name,icon,clear,bottom,tint,note}],q}`, `xray` 11-01 = `tool.xray:{title,todo,films:[{k,name,icon,img,alt,credit,intro,spots:[{n,x,y,label,kind:'inside'|'outside',t}]}],q}`, `calipers` 13-01 = `tool.calipers:{title,todo,leafImg,maxMm,groups:[{k,icon,t,short,leaves:[mm…]}],credit,q:{q,opts:[{t,ok,why}]}}`: tap a leaf, the jaws close on it, dots + averages per group) (only when a real tool fits): `{name, icon, tab, after (CSS selector to place it after), key "<WW>-tool", sim, kicker, teaser, done, why, model, modelCredit, <sim data>}` + a `SIMS.<sim>` function in the layer. `model` = a `.glb` in `assets/models/` shown with model-viewer (`assets/sparkle/vendor/model-viewer-umd.min.js`, loaded only when a student opens it). Shrink every model first: `gltf-transform optimize in.glb out.glb --compress quantize --simplify-ratio 0.35 --simplify-error 0.001 --texture-compress webp --texture-size 1024` (12.01: 10.8 MB → 1.2 MB, looks the same). Without `model`, a Sketchfab embed under manifest key `<WW>-tool` is used. |
+| `tool` | Tool of the Week (sims so far: `trailcam` 12-01, `thermometer` (cut), `berlese` 10-01 = `tool.berlese:{title,todo,parts,predict,predictFirst,days,critters,meetWin}`, `secchi` 10-02 = `tool.secchi:{title,todo,parts:[{label,t}],sites:[{k,name,icon,clear,bottom,tint,note}],q}`, `xray` 11-01 = `tool.xray:{title,todo,films:[{k,name,icon,img,alt,credit,intro,spots:[{n,x,y,label,kind:'inside'|'outside',t}]}],q}`, `calipers` 13-01 = `tool.calipers:{title,todo,leafImg,maxMm,groups:[{k,icon,t,short,leaves:[mm…]}],credit,q:{q,opts:[{t,ok,why}]}}`: tap a leaf, the jaws close on it, dots + averages per group, `dipnet` 14-01 = `tool.dipnet:{title,todo,parts:[{label,t}],spots:[{k,name,icon,where,catch:[id]}],critters:{id:{name,img,alt,stage,note}},q,credit}`) (only when a real tool fits): `{name, icon, tab, after (CSS selector to place it after), key "<WW>-tool", sim, kicker, teaser, done, why, model, modelCredit, <sim data>}` + a `SIMS.<sim>` function in the layer. `model` = a `.glb` in `assets/models/` shown with model-viewer (`assets/sparkle/vendor/model-viewer-umd.min.js`, loaded only when a student opens it). Shrink every model first: `gltf-transform optimize in.glb out.glb --compress quantize --simplify-ratio 0.35 --simplify-error 0.001 --texture-compress webp --texture-size 1024` (12.01: 10.8 MB → 1.2 MB, looks the same). Without `model`, a Sketchfab embed under manifest key `<WW>-tool` is used. |
 | `videoOff` | slots whose recorded video no longer matches the page; hidden until re-recorded (remove the slot from the list when the new take is pushed) |
 | `inputs` | On-page answers replacing "write in your notebook": types `list` (`unit`, `addLabel` rename “steps”, `title` = a prompt line above the rows) `· frame · write · pick · bank · cer · swap · hide · relabel · recap · echo · graph` (see 12-01 for each; `graph` 10-02 = tap-to-place line graph `{label,q,title,how,yLabel,ymax,ystep,step,points:[{x,lo,hi,hint}],sLabel,ph}` + a trend sentence; a text copy goes to Gathered Answers). `swap` matches innerHTML, so a phrase with <strong> inside it is better changed with a `plain` fix. |
 | `flags`, `minWords`, `hints`, `scholar` | per answer box id: "Your answer needs" chips (wide regex word lists), word counter, 3-rung hint ladder, go-further line |
